From a36fb8cd1829a8ea1b8da89167a0af2b6c311b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:03:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The guard reads the household plan's shape refusals
 (householdShapeOf), for D141's change of default

src/couplesSwitch.js householdShapeOf(plan): whether the household plan refuses a couple's plan for its shape
(src/solver/household.js householdPlanFor, on the plan src/solverCouple.js householdPlan makes, the locks applied), read
from the plan as entered with no imports, erring towards the app's rules: risks per wrapper as the engine normalises them
and the locks hold them, contributions growing at different rates, a cash ISA subscription, salaries growing at different
rates, the partner's own limits differing (partLimitsDiffer, src/solverSettings.js partCeilingsDiffer written again), one
person retired with the other paid or saving in the first year, nobody retiring within the plan. Not used by the guard yet:
D141's change of default reads it once the registered test has read.

research/tests/couple-shape.test.mjs (the full tier): over the library's 210 couples and 23 shapes each (4,830 plans), the
page's own refusal (householdCut at 'pensionsPA' on the plan it hands the solver, the mirror where the elder is entered
second) against householdShapeOf: 3,030 refused, none missed, no over-reach; each check's plant ('skip<reason>') misses
refusals of its kind (risks 210, growth 18, cashisa 60, salaries 42, limits 42, year0 144, noretire 42 on every fifth
couple). results-couple-shape.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
